  "id": "COMPOUND:30153 - PROTEIN:5792",
  "verbalization": "Methyl Lucidenate Q appears to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to RWLeu4 through a series of biochemical pathways. The first target is Ataxin-2, which is involved in a complex molecular structure that is also a target of another compound, suggesting a potential link between Methyl Lucidenate Q and the broader metabolic network it influences. The second target, Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, is involved in a pathway that ultimately directs RWLeu4, indicating a possible role in metabolic or enzymatic processes. The third target, CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, is part of a larger molecular complex that also targets RWLeu4. These findings suggest that Methyl Lucidenate Q may act through a series of interconnected molecular mechanisms, influencing key enzymes or structural proteins that ultimately lead to the formation or modification of RWLeu4. The integration of these targets highlights a potential role for Methyl Lucidenate Q in modulating metabolic or enzymatic pathways, with RWLeu4 emerging as a downstream effector in these processes.",
